  "notes": "{恐|おそ}ろしい is an i-adjective meaning frightening or terrible, stronger than {怖|こわ}い.\n\nFORMS:\n- Adverbial: {恐|おそ}ろしく\n- Noun form: {恐|おそ}ろしさ (terribleness)\n\nINTENSIFIER USE:\n{恐|おそ}ろしく + adjective/adverb means 'terribly, incredibly':\n- {恐|おそ}ろしく{速|はや}い: terribly fast\n- {恐|おそ}ろしく{高|たか}い: incredibly expensive\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {怖|こわ}い: scary, afraid (more common in daily speech)\n- {恐怖|きょうふ}: fear, terror (noun)\n- {物|もの}{凄|すご}い: tremendous, incredible\n\nNOTE:\nIn colloquial use, {恐|おそ}ろしい can express amazement at something extreme, not necessarily fear.",
